E AX3076 1018-effect-tag-list.ax:16:6-11 effect-tag-list "`effect(io, unsafe)` on `comma` names 2 effects, and an `effect(...)` tag names one" #"one effect per `effect(...)` tag" !"a list here was read as ONE effect spelled with the comma in it, which nothing declares - so the claim could never be satisfied, and AX3010 reported it missing from a body that performed it. `restrict(...)` takes a comma list; `effect(...)` does not" ?"write one tag line per effect: `;@axiom:effect(io)` and `;@axiom:effect(unsafe)`"
E AX3042 1018-effect-tag-list.ax:16:6-11 undeclared-effect "`comma` performs IO and its declaration does not say so" !"effects are INFERRED transitively, so this fires on every function up the call chain, and each one is a place a reader would otherwise have to open the callee to learn it. If the effect is not wanted here the fix is to stop performing it, not to stop saying so. `IO`, `Entropy`, `Spawn` and `Block` are required; `Alloc` and `Mut` are ambient and never need declaring" ?16:1:"write `;@axiom:effect(io)` above the declaration"~>";@axiom:effect(io)\n"
E AX3073 1018-effect-tag-list.ax:19:6-14 undeclared-unsafe "`comma` touches raw memory and its declaration does not say so" #"__load64" ?16:1:"write `;@axiom:effect(unsafe)` above the declaration"~>";@axiom:effect(unsafe)\n" ?"this fires where the unsafe operation is performed, not up the call chain. The tag makes the declaration a trusted encapsulation, whose callers inherit nothing. If the operation is not wanted here the fix is to stop performing it, not to stop saying so"
E AX3076 1018-effect-tag-list.ax:24:6-11 effect-tag-list "`effect(io unsafe)` on `blank` names 2 effects, and an `effect(...)` tag names one" #"one effect per `effect(...)` tag" !"a list here was read as ONE effect spelled with the comma in it, which nothing declares - so the claim could never be satisfied, and AX3010 reported it missing from a body that performed it. `restrict(...)` takes a comma list; `effect(...)` does not" ?"write one tag line per effect: `;@axiom:effect(io)` and `;@axiom:effect(unsafe)`"
E AX3042 1018-effect-tag-list.ax:24:6-11 undeclared-effect "`blank` performs IO and its declaration does not say so" !"effects are INFERRED transitively, so this fires on every function up the call chain, and each one is a place a reader would otherwise have to open the callee to learn it. If the effect is not wanted here the fix is to stop performing it, not to stop saying so. `IO`, `Entropy`, `Spawn` and `Block` are required; `Alloc` and `Mut` are ambient and never need declaring" ?24:1:"write `;@axiom:effect(io)` above the declaration"~>";@axiom:effect(io)\n"
E AX3073 1018-effect-tag-list.ax:27:6-14 undeclared-unsafe "`blank` touches raw memory and its declaration does not say so" #"__load64" ?24:1:"write `;@axiom:effect(unsafe)` above the declaration"~>";@axiom:effect(unsafe)\n" ?"this fires where the unsafe operation is performed, not up the call chain. The tag makes the declaration a trusted encapsulation, whose callers inherit nothing. If the operation is not wanted here the fix is to stop performing it, not to stop saying so"
